"77_array_species.mst — MACDART: Array>>select:/reject: answer an Array.

 21_collections_ext.mst deliberately gives the abstract Collection a select:/
 reject:/collect: that always build a plain OrderedCollection (its untyped model
 stripped the species machinery). Array already keeps its OWN collect: override
 (10_array.mst) that answers an Array — so as shipped `#(1 2) collect:` is an
 Array but `#(1 2) select:` is an OrderedCollection, an inconsistency inside the
 one class. This overlay finishes the species contract for Array the same way
 (Squeak/ANSI: Array>>select: answers an Array), by collecting into an
 OrderedCollection then answering its asArray. Loads after 10/21 (file 77), so
 reopen replaces Collection's inherited select:/reject: for Array receivers only;
 OrderedCollection/Set/Interval keep the OrderedCollection-returning versions."

Array >> select: aBlock [
    | r |
    r := OrderedCollection new.
    self do: [:each | (aBlock value: each) ifTrue: [ r add: each ] ].
    ^r asArray
]
Array >> reject: aBlock [
    ^self select: [:each | (aBlock value: each) not ]
]
